---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { business } from "../data/site";

const updated = "September 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Top Order Digital collects, uses and looks after your personal information."
  stickyCta={false}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1 style="margin-top:1.25rem">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="prose__updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This site is run by {business.owner}, trading as {business.name}
        (ABN {business.abn}), a sole trader based in {business.suburb}. This
        policy explains what personal information I collect through
        {business.domain}, why, and what I do with it. I follow the Australian
        Privacy Principles in the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth).
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <p>
        The only information I collect is what you send me through the enquiry
        form or by email: your name, business name and trade, the suburbs you
        work in, your phone number if you give it, and whatever you write in
        your message.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site does not use analytics or advertising cookies. My host
        (Cloudflare) keeps standard server logs — IP address, browser type,
        pages requested — for security and to keep the site running, and counts
        visits and page load times without cookies. I don't use any of that to
        identify individuals.
      </p>
      <p>
        The body text font is loaded from Google Fonts, so when a page opens,
        your browser fetches it from Google's servers and Google receives your
        IP address and browser details. Google handles that under its own
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How I use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To read your enquiry and reply to it.</li>
        <li>To quote on and, if you go ahead, deliver your website.</li>
        <li>To keep in touch about work I'm doing for you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I don't send marketing emails, and I never sell or rent your
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it's shared with</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiry-form submissions are delivered to my inbox through Web3Forms, a
        form-handling service. Your message is also stored in my email
        (Google). If I build your site, I may use hosting, domain and email
        providers on your behalf — I'll tell you which ones. I only share your
        information where it's needed to do the work, or where the law requires
        it. Web3Forms, Google and Cloudflare may store or handle information
        outside Australia.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        I keep enquiry emails while there's a reasonable chance we'll work
        together, and project records for as long as I need them for tax and
        business records (generally five to seven years). You can ask me to
        delete your enquiry at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Access, correction and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see what personal information I hold about you, ask me to
        correct it, or ask me to delete it. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> and I'll sort
        it out. If you're not happy with how I've handled your information, you
        can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au">oaic.gov.au</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version goes up on this page with an
        updated date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
